 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484193 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484087 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484193 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82287" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484193 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484193 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $5det(A)+2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 1.5 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484193 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "00ee9625-b07b-5511-af62-7520bef2fbbd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484193 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has proportional rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -1 & 1.5 \\\\ 3 & -9 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- For the matrix $B,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(B)=2\\cdot 3-\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $5det(A)+2det(B)=5\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 3=6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484213 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484213 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82194" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484213 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484213 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 3\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0.5 \\\\ 3 & -3 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484213 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3d069a94-d7d6-5988-ba00-dc610c0a1a5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484213 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has identical columns: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -1 & -7 \\\\ 3 & 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|A|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero row: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 & 0.5 \\\\ 3 & -3 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- Since $C$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|C|=7\\cdot (-1)\\cdot (-2)=14\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $|A|$ and $|B|$ are equal to $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484278 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186484165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484278 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82193" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484278 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484278 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following determinants are equal to $0?$\n\n$$\n|A|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|,\\,|B|=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|,\\,|C|=|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484278 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf8a8a57-6cfe-5981-b026-15b496e6e0d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186484278 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's examine each of the given determinants in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ is a triangular matrix, we obtain \n\n$$\n|A|=5\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 2=-10\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ has a zero column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|B|=0.$\n\n- The matrix $C$ has identical rows: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nAs a result, $|C|=0.$\n\nTherefore, only $|B|$ and $|C|$ are equal to $0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
